{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHz9mPCDZiF3iWEbEWWYsX","type":"tool_result","content":"1	/**
2	 * Durable, host-independent ownership boundary for cross-provider CLI runs.
3	 *
4	 * A caller submits a sealed spec plus one-shot prompt capability, then a
5	 * detached worker claims it and owns the provider process until an exclusive
6	 * terminal record is written. Callers may attach, poll, disappear, or return;
7	 * none of those events owns provider liveness. In particular, output silence
8	 * is not a terminal signal. Every run instead has a finite absolute deadline
9	 * and is reconciled on the next status/cancel/attach touch.
10	 */
