n one batch and 5/6 failing in another), which is why it survived earlier rounds whose recorded evidence claims a focused/aggregate PASS. The story's own top-level aggregate suite `managed-cross-provider-suite-smoke` FAILS at current HEAD f7b3bb27e1 through this same assertion, contradicting the recorded aggregate-PASS evidence bound to an earlier commit. Operator-visible impact is real and not cosmetic: handlers/host-run.ts:200 maps this terminal to exit code 130 (cancelled) instead of 124 (timed_out), and :211-216 then report timedOut=false, timeoutKind=null, terminalReason='aborted', failureKind='unknown' for a run that actually exhausted its absolute deadline; handlers/cross-host-review.ts:750 likewise misses its `run.state === 'timed_out' ? 124` branch and reports timedOut=false. This directly undercuts the CHK-001/CHK-003 contract that a silent-but-live provider converges to definite timed_out terminal truth, and makes an operator deciding recovery/replacement from the receipt see an operator cancellation where the deadline actually fired. Fix: derive the state from the cancel reason in both worker branches exactly as the reconciler already does.","severity":"high","category":"adversarial","evidenceState":"verified","files":["packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts","packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/handlers/cross-host-review.ts","packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-command-smoke.ts"]}],"note":"Story-level quality review of the integrated change at HEAD f7b3bb27e1. One high-severity confirmed defect registered (worker terminal-state misclassification writing state=cancelled with reason=absolute_deadline_exceeded, reproduced with captured on-disk artifacts and a failing story-owned aggregate suite). Clean on the role's other check items: tsc --noEmit passes for packages/main; no `as any`, no empty/swallowing catch blocks, and no unused imports in the new core modules (managed-host-run.ts, managed-review-evidence.ts, provider-pr